.DS_Store
# Harness probes are per-machine canary state and stay local. Run journals are
# committed: this repository records its own runs, and a journal nobody can read
# is evidence nobody can check. Prompt text is kept OUT of them by
# NULLIUS_WITNESS_PROMPTS=0 in .claude/settings.json — a prompt record carries
# its length and hash, which proves a turn happened without publishing what was
# typed. If that setting is ever removed, journals start carrying verbatim
# prompts into a public repository and nothing will say so.
# Fixtures meant to be read live under spec/fixtures/ and are committed too.
.nullius/probes/

# Retrospectives are candid internal records of how a run actually went.
# Publishing one changes what gets written into it, so they stay local; the
# next run's retro-writer reads them from the working tree either way.
.claude/retrospectives/*.md
